Third-party code in draco_decoder.wasm

draco_decoder.wasm is a WebAssembly (wasm32-wasip1) build of the mesh
decoder of Google Draco 1.5.7 (https://github.com/google/draco; copyright
Google Inc. and other contributors, per its AUTHORS file). It is compiled
from the unmodified Draco 1.5.7 sources plus the wrapper
tools/draco-wasm/draco_wasi.cc by tools/draco-wasm/build-draco-wasm.sh,
which pins and checksums every input.

Draco is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Its license file
is LICENSE-draco in this directory, copied unchanged from the Draco 1.5.7
source tree; its last section covers a documentation script of the Draco
repository that is not part of the decoder. Draco ships no NOTICE file.

The module also contains the parts of the wasi-sdk 34 sysroot it links
(wasi-libc and the LLVM C++ runtime). The wasi-sdk 34 release archive
carries no license files, and their license texts are not reproduced here
yet.

internal/draco runs the module with wazero (github.com/tetratelabs/wazero
v1.12.0, Apache License, Version 2.0), a Go module dependency compiled into
the rodin3d-mcp binary. wazero's NOTICE file reads:

